  "solution": {
    "text": "H-atom directly attached with 'P' atom is reducing in nature. H-atom attached with P atom through oxygen atom is acidic in nature. <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0095_c09d048abd8c.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.20833in;height:1.28333in\"> <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0095_056bc7b76098.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.49167in;height:1.50833in\"> <br/>Only orthophosphoric acid <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> has H-atom directly attached with 'P' atom, therefore, it is reducing in nature. Rest other are oxidising agents."
